# 15. DOUBLE-BOOKING PROTECTION

This is critical.

Two users must not be able to book the same final available slot simultaneously.

Use database-level protection/transaction logic.

Booking process:

1. Begin transaction.
2. Lock/check slot.
3. Verify availability.
4. Create site visit.
5. Increment booking count.
6. Commit transaction.

If another booking takes the slot first:

Return:

> "That slot was just booked. Here are the next available times."

Never show a successful booking when the database rejected it.

